  "title": "Learn to Recognize Vague or Overly General Statements",
  "description": "Learn to recognize vague or overly general statements. Here’s how: - Ask for specifics: If a description feels “too true,” ask, “What exactly do you mean?” - Compare with others: Check if others find the same statement equally relatable. - Stay skeptical: Remind yourself that generalities aren’t personalized insights. Example: If a personality test tells you, “You value connection but also enjoy solitude,” notice how universally applicable that is.",
